# Git Rules

- Do not commit unless the human asks
- Keep commits focused; avoid mixing refactors with features
- Never commit `.env`, keys, credentials, or large binaries
- Do not amend pushed history or force-push shared branches unless explicitly requested
- Prefer clear commit messages that explain why
- Before finishing: review `git diff` for accidental files

See `docs/conventions/git.md`
